    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1">

                <pb facs="0127" n="1" sameAs="frus:frus1925v01/pg1"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A4b/301</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of the Navy</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Wilbur</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi><anchor n="2" xml:id="d1-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-02-17"><hi rendition="#italic">February 17,
                        1925</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">29440–178:17S</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I take pleasure in advising you that this
                    Department has completed the work of the scrapping of vessels required to be
                    demolished under the Treaty Limiting Naval Armament.</p>
                <p>Under the provisions of the Treaty the Battle Cruisers <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Lexington</hi> and <hi rendition="#italic">Saratoga</hi> are being
                    converted into airplane carriers and the Battleship <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >North Dakota</hi> is being retained as a target.</p>
                <p>Respectfully,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Curtis D. Wilbur</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1-f1" n="2" type="source" xml:id="d1-f1-content">
                <p>In telegrams dated Feb. 17, 6 p.m., the information contained in this letter was
                    communicated to the Embassies in France, Great Britain, Italy, and Japan, with
                    instructions to convey it to the respective Governments.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
